    "result_text": "The build is green with the only test class passing.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` behaviour with minimal structural impact, adding new cohesive units rather than growing existing methods/classes.\n\n**What the feature does:** When a create request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, the endpoint allows an owner at an address already used by a same-lastName owner (already handled by the existing `RejectDuplicateHousehold`'s opt-in early return) and now assigns the new owner \u2014 plus every existing same-lastName owner at that address \u2014 the same stable `householdId`, then returns it.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`AssignHousehold.java`** (new): one small function class with a single `service` method. Derives the `householdId` deterministically from the normalised last name + address (`String.format(\"HH-%08X\", \u2026)`), so all household members compute the identical, stable value; sets it on the built owner and on matching existing owners. New class \u2192 zero surrounding complexity.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`**: inserted one `assignHousehold` step between `assignCustomerCode` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n- **`Owner.java`**: added the `householdId` field plus a two-line getter/setter (new methods; no existing method touched).\n- **`openapi.yml`**: added `householdId` as a read-only property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically (no mapper change).\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`data.sql`**: added the `household_id` column and the matching trailing `NULL` in the 10 seed inserts. (h2 needs no change \u2014 it relies on `ddl-auto=update`.)\n\nThe `RejectDuplicateHousehold` step and the mapper were left untouched. The acceptance test (`coreJoinersShareHouseholdId`) and the full suite pass.",
